Subject: [M156] [Passwords] Reset driver state on cross-document navigations

Original change's description:
> [Passwords] Reset driver state on cross-document navigations
>
> A cross-document navigation can reuse the frame's RenderFrameHost
> (e.g. when leaving the initial empty document), so the
> ContentPasswordManagerDriver is reused too. When a navigation commits a
> new document (i.e. not for BFCache restores or prerender activations),
> invalidate the driver's weak pointers, assign a new DriverId, and reset
> its PasswordGenerationFrameHelper and PasswordAutofillManager (incl.
> pending callbacks and its own suggestions), so the new document starts
> with fresh state.
>
> Also rename PasswordAutofillManager::DidNavigateMainFrame() to
> DidNavigateFrame().
>
